# E2E testIDs (Maestro)

Whenever you add or change interactive UI in this app, include stable `testID` props so Maestro flows can be written without a new native rebuild.

## Naming

- Screens: `screen-{name}` — e.g. `screen-home`, `screen-route`
- Tabs: `tab-{TabName}` — already on `CurvedTabBar`
- Actions: `{area}-{action}` — e.g. `route-add-more`, `settings-sign-in`
- Fields: `{area}-{field}` — e.g. `login-email`, `chat-input`
- List rows: `{entity}-{id}` — e.g. `attraction-card-${id}`, `saved-route-${id}`
- Nested actions on a row: `{entity}-{action}-${id}` — e.g. `attraction-add-${id}`

Use lowercase kebab-case. Prefer stable IDs over index-based IDs.

## What needs a testID

- Screen root `SafeAreaView` / main container
- Primary / secondary buttons
- Text inputs and submit
- Tabs, sheets, modals, empty-state CTAs
- Cards users tap; include Add / Details / Delete when present
- Error helpers that tests assert on (`login-error`)

## What to skip

- Purely decorative views
- Every tiny `Text` label (title/key CTA is enough)
- Changing existing IDs unless fixing a bug (breaks flows)

## Checklist before finishing a UI task

1. New screen → `testID="screen-..."` on root
2. New button / input → `testID`
3. New list item component → id-suffixed `testID`
4. If you add a user journey, note it under `docs/E2E_FLOWS.md` as a TODO flow if no YAML exists yet

See `docs/E2E.md` (how to run) and `docs/E2E_FLOWS.md` (flow backlog + ID map).
